	(text "WSNES cart v0.3 - mixed SMD/THT, standard SNES PCB shape (ESP32-S3 + 512 KB ROM-SRAM + battery-backed save RAM, LoROM)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 3 3) (thickness 0.6) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fdb64a63-674c-5a23-a6b8-406731ffd6ca")
	)
	(text "Save RAM: AS6C1008 at LoROM $70-$7D/$F0-$FF:0000-7FFF, CR2032 backed, write-protected below 4.4 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 345.44 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "30ba3876-fe17-5d75-a61f-2d2389977fe8")
	)
	(text "SAVE RAM\nU17 decodes the LoROM save area: A22=A21=A20=1, A15=0, /ROMSEL=0 -> SAVE_SEL_N (only in SNES mode and when SAVE_EN=1).\nU19 masks A11-A14 with SAVE_M11..M14 (ESP GPIOs) so the RAM mirrors at the header size (2 KB: all 0, 8 KB: M11+M12, 32 KB: all 1).\nSome games check the mirroring (anti-copier), so set the masks from the ROM header before releasing reset.\nESP access: BUS_ESP=1, address bit EA19 (U11 QD) = 1 selects the save chip, 0 the ROM chip (set masks to 1 for full access).\nPower fail: U20 drives CE2 low below ~4.4 V, R7 holds it low when the cart is off -> no garbage writes, data kept by BT1.\nEvery SNES write to the save area pulses MBX_IRQ_N -> ESP knows the save is dirty and copies it to SD (.srm) on reset/game change."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 360.68 355.6 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "92e73079-9aac-59dc-96f5-f6dc5944f8ec")
	)
	(text "SNES edge + SuperCIC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "04ee2369-f47e-59c7-b76b-55b821e1b5f7")
	)
	(text "SNES-side bus buffers (5 V, enabled when BUS_ESP = 0)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.08 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3349a22-deda-5d5c-a1d1-0cc56e08517e")
	)
	(text "SRAM + bus-ownership glue"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.68 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "75d3eebc-4b1f-51b7-80a2-3268a030e224")
	)
	(text "ESP-side serial address/data access (5 V HCT)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 335.28 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "215f4919-8736-55f7-ae47-041073ea50fb")
	)
	(text "5V->3V3 + reset + pull-ups"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "82e7f8b0-e566-51e3-a99c-3c617bb2e7d7")
	)
	(text "ESP32-S3-WROOM-1 (hand-soldered) + microSD + USB-C + 3V3 LDO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 518.16 27.94 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "275b33a4-8f11-5502-9e3b-2dcf1f8319b6")
	)
	(text "Assembly field: JLC = SMD assembled by JLCPCB, HAND = you solder it (U21 ESP module, U15 PIC, BT1, J3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 33.48 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5ee361a1-1e34-597b-aa8e-7d35638cbcf1")
	)
	(text "Power + decoupling (one 100 nF per IC, place at VCC pin)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 290.83 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2 2) (thickness 0.4) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1c961cef-a1cb-5df1-a792-c239ffce877c")
	)
	(text "BUS OWNERSHIP (single GPIO BUS_ESP, pulled HIGH = ESP owns bus at power-up)\nBUS_ESP=0 (SNES plays): U2-U4 drive SA*, U5 passes data when ROM_SEL_N=0,\n   SRAM /CE=ROM_SEL_N, /OE=SNES /RD, /WE=SNES_WE_N (only if MENU_WE_N=0).\nBUS_ESP=1 (ESP loads): U9-U11 drive SA*, U12 drives SD* when DOUT_OE_N=0,\n   ROM /CE=EA19, save /CE1=NOT EA19, /OE=ESP_OE_N, /WE=ESP_WE_N. U13 reads SD* back via SPI MISO.\nLoROM decode: ROM_SEL_N = /ROMSEL OR NOT A15. SNES A16-A19 -> SRAM A15-A18.\nWrites: SNES_WE_N = /WR OR (SAVE_SEL_N AND (ROM_SEL_N OR MENU_WE_N)) -> save area always, ROM area only in menu mode.\nReset: Q1 pulls SNES /RESET low (gate pulled up = SNES held in reset until ESP firmware releases it).\nMailbox: with MENU_WE_N=0 the menu may write into SRAM; each write pulses MBX_IRQ_N to the ESP."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.68 280 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d6c40209-ec9e-50e2-8154-de834728542b")
	)
	(text "ESP32-S3 GPIO MAP (N16R8: GPIO35-37 are used by octal PSRAM - do not use!)\nGPIO4 BUS_ESP   GPIO5 ESP_WE_N   GPIO6 ESP_OE_N   GPIO7 DOUT_OE_N\nGPIO15 RD_LOAD_N  GPIO16 MENU_WE_N  GPIO17 SNES_RST_DRV (1 = hold SNES in reset)\nGPIO18 MBX_IRQ_N  GPIO8 RESET_SENSE_N  GPIO9 SNES_5V_SENSE\nSPI2 (IOMUX): GPIO10 SR_LATCH, GPIO11 SR_MOSI, GPIO12 SR_SCK, GPIO13 SR_MISO\nSD (SPI3): GPIO1 CS, GPIO2 SCK, GPIO42 MOSI, GPIO41 MISO, GPIO38 card detect (0 = card in)\nUSB: GPIO19/20 native USB (flashing + serial), GPIO0 BOOT button, GPIO48 status LED\nSave RAM: GPIO21 SAVE_EN, GPIO14 M11, GPIO47 M12, GPIO39 M13, GPIO40 M14\nShift order (MSB first, 32 bit): DATA[7:0], A[23:16] (bit19 = EA19 save select), A[15:8], A[7:0]\nNever drive 5 V-side outputs while SNES_5V_SENSE = 0 (USB-only power: only the ESP side is alive)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 424.18 280 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "eb3afc0a-4cd1-5f77-9f18-078d37e09689")
	)
